  "authors": "Dr. Sarah Johnson, Dr. Michael Chen, Dr. Lisa Rodriguez",
  "funding": "NIH R01DA045678; SAMHSA TI123456",
  "abstract": "This intensive longitudinal study examines real-time recovery processes among adults with substance use disorders. Participants complete ecological momentary assessments 10 times daily for 28 days, capturing dynamic fluctuations in craving, affect, stress, coping, and contextual factors. A comprehensive baseline assessment characterizes demographic, socioeconomic, and clinical history variables.",
